class @beta Efl.Ui.Image_Factory extends Efl.Ui.Caching_Factory
{
   [[An @Efl.Ui.Factory that builds @Efl.Ui.Image objects from a model.

     Bind a model property with @Efl.Ui.Property_Bind.property_bind and the
     images it names are what the view shows. The key says what the property
     holds: "filename" (or no key) for a file's path, "icon" for an icon's
     name, as @Efl.Ui.Image.icon takes it. Being an @Efl.Ui.Caching_Factory,
     it keeps the objects it has built for reuse, which is what makes
     scrolling a long list of images affordable.
   ]]
   implements {
      Efl.Object.constructor;
      Efl.Object.destructor;
      Efl.Ui.Factory.create;
      Efl.Ui.Property_Bind.property_bind;
   }
}
